{"id":"lwyieev2pl831akmivvxvox9v","title":"植物如何感知温度：COP1 蛋白充当温度开关","originalTitle":"Plants feel the heat: How a protein 'thermometer' helps plants adapt to climate","summary":"研究发现植物分子调节器 COP1 通过其内部温度开关调节活性，温度升高时 COP1 结构变化，促进生长相关蛋白的降解，从而促进植物适应高温环境。不同植物物种中 COP1 的灵活性差异反映了其对温度变化的敏感性不同，这一发现有助于作物适应更热的气候。","reason":null,"source":{"name":"Phys.org"},"links":{"original":"https://phys.org/news/2026-11-protein-thermometer-climate.html"},"publishedAt":"2026-11-11T16:20:01.000Z","discoveredAt":"2026-11-11T16:20:45.361Z","timelineAt":"2026-11-11T16:20:45.361Z","category":"life-science","tags":["研究成果","蛋白质结构"],"score":38,"selected":false,"channel":"news","story":{"publicId":"e26a7c6c-4392-4c10-9cd4-7814f1f5dc16","title":"COP1蛋白温度响应机制研究揭示物种间差异"},"x":null,"readingMode":"full","author":null,"body":null,"outline":[],"relatedStories":[{"publicId":"e26a7c6c-4392-4c10-9cd4-7814f1f5dc16","title":"COP1蛋白温度响应机制研究揭示物种间差异"}],"topics":[{"slug":"protein-structure","name":"蛋白质结构与设计"}],"indexable":false,"markdownAvailable":true,"group":{"factId":"fK4aJkdZX9kE","reportCount":1,"additionalSourceCount":0},"hasTranslation":false,"bodyLanguage":"original"}